#
# Counter-example for math:DegenerateZigzagDiagramConstraint (issue #1527): a
# math:ZigzagDiagram whose every math:zigzagArrow points FORWARD (math:forwardArrow) —
# no math:backwardArrow at all — so it has collapsed to ordinary forward-only
# single-parameter persistence. The guarded-existence constraint (a zigzag diagram must
# have at least one arrow whose math:arrowDirection is math:backwardArrow) fires —
# shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent (math:DegenerateZigzagDiagram).
# ISOLATION: the diagram and its arrows are otherwise well-formed; the only defect is the
# absence of a backward arrow, so EXACTLY ONE finding.
# Back-reference: math:DegenerateZigzagDiagram (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecZigzagForwardOnly).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:forwardOnly a math:ZigzagDiagram ;
    math:zigzagArrow ex:arrow01 , ex:arrow12 .

# Every arrow points forward — no math:backwardArrow, so the zigzag is degenerate.
ex:arrow01 a math:Morphism ; math:arrowDirection math:forwardArrow .
ex:arrow12 a math:Morphism ; math:arrowDirection math:forwardArrow .
